1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,897
The first promise was made in the clinic canteen, over a plate of salad and a bowl of soup.

2
00:00:05,897 --> 00:00:11,862
“Make the site accessible, or we stop the run,” Maya said.

3
00:00:11,862 --> 00:00:27,989
“That is the immediate step.” The custom in that place was to bring your own sauce, and the sweet vinegar in a little jar became, in their argument, a way of speaking about the degree of trouble they were in.

4
00:00:27,989 --> 00:00:41,342
The situation was simple: the incidence of ankle injuries had doubled, the tray of bandages was always empty, and the physiotherapist had restricted the training to short sessions.

5
00:00:41,342 --> 00:00:46,027
“Take the wrist and the ankle seriously,” she said.

6
00:00:46,027 --> 00:00:55,796
“A bump ignored becomes a deficiency.” Far from being late, the intervention was exactly on time.

7
00:00:55,796 --> 00:01:09,348
They sent a form to the management and involved the orchestra of the sports club in a formation that took a quantitative view: an ounce of prevention, a pinch of salt, a gallon of water.

8
00:01:09,348 --> 00:01:13,583
“Understand the derivation,” the coach said.

9
00:01:13,583 --> 00:01:22,982
“An approximation is not a plan.” The sticky floor of the changing room was the first item on the list.

10
00:01:22,982 --> 00:01:34,730
The interference came from a dietary habit nobody wanted to discuss: the players chewed fast, ate standing, and stopped only when the whistle blew.

11
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:42,229
“Dumb animals eat better than we do,” the goalkeeper said, and the pigeon on the windowsill agreed.

12
00:01:42,229 --> 00:01:49,268
The ending of the old diet had to be an outbreak of honesty, not a slogan.

13
00:01:49,268 --> 00:02:01,986
The promised improvements were small and regular: a regularity of meals, a disposal of the old rules, a shrink in the menu, and the flesh of two oranges a day.

14
00:02:01,986 --> 00:02:06,381
“Bring the ladder and take the walk,” Daniel said.

15
00:02:06,381 --> 00:02:16,309
“I understand the way now.” It was a ruinous habit they were fighting, and they would fight it through an Olympiad of small mornings.

16
00:02:16,309 --> 00:02:21,364
The fact was that the club had lost contact with its own members.

17
00:02:21,364 --> 00:02:33,382
An intrusion of sponsors into the medical room, a sweet sauce on every plate, and a bowl of salad that nobody ate: the culture of the place had to change.

18
00:02:33,382 --> 00:02:37,776
“Take the tray and send the message,” she said.

19
00:02:37,776 --> 00:02:43,838
“Situation by situation, that is the only way.”
